from lib import *
C=10;S='maths';CH='numbers-and-sequences'
lesson(C,S,CH,'sequences-and-arithmetic-progression',"Sequences and Arithmetic Progression (AP)","Steps of a staircase","Each step of a staircase is 15 cm higher than the one below. The heights 15, 30, 45, 60 ... follow a pattern: add the same amount each time.",
["A sequence is a list of numbers arranged in a definite order, such as 2, 4, 6, 8, ... Each number is a term. @ sequence",
 "A sequence in which each term is obtained by adding a fixed number d to the previous term is an Arithmetic Progression (AP). @ AP",
 "The fixed number d is the common difference: d = t2 - t1 = t3 - t2. It can be positive, negative or zero. @ common difference d",
 "If the first term is a and the common difference d, the AP is a, a + d, a + 2d, ... @ a, a + d, a + 2d",
 "The general (n-th) term is t_n = a + (n - 1)d. @ t_n = a + (n - 1)d",
 "For the AP 5, 8, 11, ... we have a = 5, d = 3, so t_10 = 5 + 9 x 3 = 32. @ t_10 = 32",
 "Three numbers a, b, c are in AP exactly when 2b = a + c, that is b is the average of its neighbours. @ 2b = a + c"],
("Which term of the AP 3, 8, 13, 18, ... is 78?",[("a = 3 and d = 5. Use t_n = a + (n - 1)d = 78.","Identify a and d first."),("3 + (n - 1) x 5 = 78, so (n - 1) x 5 = 75 and n - 1 = 15.","Solve the equation for n."),("n = 16. So 78 is the 16th term.","n must be a positive whole number.")]),
("State the formula for the n-th term of an AP and say how you find d.",["t_n = a + (n - 1)d","d is the difference of consecutive terms","Three numbers are in AP if 2b = a + c"],["Using n instead of n - 1"]),
["An AP adds a fixed common difference d each time.","t_n = a + (n - 1)d.","a, b, c are in AP if 2b = a + c.","d can be negative: 20, 17, 14 has d = -3."],
["n|Common difference of 7, 11, 15, 19 is|4|11 - 7 = 4.",
 "m|The 10th term of 2, 5, 8, ... is|29|27~Use a + 9d = 2 + 27;30~Use n - 1 = 9|2 + 9 x 3 = 29.",
 "t|1, 2, 4, 8 is an AP.|False|Differences 1, 2, 4 are not equal.",
 "n|Find the 15th term of 4, 9, 14, ...|74|4 + 14 x 5 = 74.",
 "t|-5, -8, -11 is an AP with d = -3.|True|Each term is 3 less than the previous.",
 "m|If a = 10, d = 3, then t_5 =|22|25~t_5 = a + 4d;13~Multiply 4 by 3 and add 10|10 + 4 x 3 = 22.",
 "n|Which term of 5, 11, 17, ... is 53? Give n.|9|5 + (n-1)6 = 53, n = 9.",
 "t|Three numbers a, b, c are in AP when 2b = a + c.|True|b is the average of a and c."])
lesson(C,S,CH,'series-and-sum-of-ap',"Series and the sum of an AP","Gauss and the class","A teacher once asked a class to add 1 + 2 + 3 + ... + 100. A boy named Gauss answered in seconds. He paired 1 with 100, 2 with 99 and so on - fifty pairs each making 101.",
["A series is the sum of the terms of a sequence, for example 1 + 3 + 5 + 7. @ series",
 "For an AP with first term a, common difference d and n terms, the sum is S_n = n/2 x [2a + (n - 1)d]. @ S_n = n/2[2a + (n-1)d]",
 "If the last term l is known, S_n = n/2 x (a + l). @ S_n = n/2(a + l)",
 "Check with Gauss: n = 100, a = 1, l = 100, so S = 100/2 x 101 = 5050. @ 5050",
 "The sum of the first n natural numbers is n(n + 1)/2. @ n(n+1)/2",
 "The sum of the first n odd numbers is n squared, and of the first n even numbers is n(n + 1). @ odd numbers: n^2",
 "Also t_n = S_n - S_(n-1), so we can find any term from the sum formula. @ t_n = S_n - S_(n-1)"],
("Find the sum of the first 20 terms of the AP 4, 7, 10, ...",[("a = 4, d = 3, n = 20.","Read off a, d, n."),("S_20 = 20/2 x [2 x 4 + 19 x 3] = 10 x [8 + 57] = 10 x 65.","Substitute in the formula."),("S_20 = 650.","Multiply carefully.")]),
("How did Gauss add 1 to 100 so quickly, and what formula follows?",["Pair first and last terms","Each pair makes 101","S_n = n/2 (a + l)"],["Forgetting to halve n"]),
["S_n = n/2 [2a + (n - 1)d] = n/2 (a + l).","1 + 2 + ... + n = n(n + 1)/2.","Sum of first n odd numbers = n squared.","t_n = S_n - S_(n-1)."],
["n|1 + 2 + 3 + ... + 10 =|55|10 x 11 / 2 = 55.",
 "n|Sum of the first 5 odd numbers is|25|5 squared = 25.",
 "m|Sum of the first n natural numbers is|n(n+1)/2|n squared~That is for odd numbers;n(n-1)/2~Check with n = 3: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6|3 x 4 / 2 = 6.",
 "n|Find S_10 of the AP 2, 4, 6, ...|110|10/2 x (4 + 9 x 2) = 110.",
 "t|The sum formula S_n = n/2 (a + l) needs the last term l.|True|It uses the first and last terms.",
 "n|Sum of 5, 10, 15, ..., 50 is|275|10/2 x (5 + 50) = 275.",
 "n|If S_n = 3n squared, find t_1 (that is S_1).|3|3 x 1 squared = 3.",
 "n|Sum of the first 100 natural numbers is|5050|100 x 101 / 2."])
lesson(C,S,CH,'geometric-progression',"Geometric Progression (GP) and its sum","The bouncing ball","A ball dropped from 64 cm rebounds to half its previous height each time: 64, 32, 16, 8 ... Here we multiply by the same number each time instead of adding.",
["A sequence in which each term is obtained by multiplying the previous term by a fixed non-zero number r is a Geometric Progression (GP). @ GP",
 "The fixed multiplier r is the common ratio: r = t2 / t1 = t3 / t2. @ common ratio r",
 "A GP with first term a is a, ar, ar squared, ar cubed, ... @ a, ar, ar^2",
 "The n-th term is t_n = a r^(n-1). @ t_n = a r^(n-1)",
 "Three non-zero numbers a, b, c are in GP exactly when b squared = ac. @ b^2 = ac",
 "The sum of n terms is S_n = a (r^n - 1)/(r - 1) when r is greater than 1, and S_n = a (1 - r^n)/(1 - r) when r is less than 1. @ S_n",
 "If r = 1 then S_n = n x a. @ r = 1"],
("Find the 8th term of the GP 3, 6, 12, ... and the sum of its first 5 terms.",[("a = 3, r = 2. t_8 = 3 x 2^7 = 3 x 128 = 384.","Use t_n = a r^(n-1)."),("S_5 = 3 (2^5 - 1)/(2 - 1) = 3 x 31.","r is greater than 1, so use (r^n - 1)/(r - 1)."),("S_5 = 93.","Check: 3 + 6 + 12 + 24 + 48 = 93.")]),
("What is the difference between an AP and a GP?",["AP adds a fixed d","GP multiplies by a fixed r","Formulae t_n = a + (n-1)d and t_n = a r^(n-1)"],["Mixing up the two formulae"]),
["GP: multiply by a fixed ratio r.","t_n = a r^(n-1).","S_n = a (r^n - 1)/(r - 1) for r greater than 1.","a, b, c in GP means b squared = ac."],
["n|Common ratio of 2, 6, 18, 54 is|3|6 / 2 = 3.",
 "t|1, 4, 9, 16 is a GP.|False|Ratios 4, 2.25, ... are not equal.",
 "n|8th term of 1, 2, 4, ... is|128|2^7 = 128.",
 "n|Sum of 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 is|15|1 x (2^4 - 1)/(2 - 1) = 15.",
 "m|If a = 5, r = 3, then t_3 =|45|15~t_3 = a r squared;27~Multiply by 5 too|5 x 9 = 45.",
 "t|Three numbers a, b, c in GP satisfy b squared = ac.|True|b is the geometric mean.",
 "n|If 3, x, 12 are in GP (x positive), x =|6|x squared = 36.",
 "n|Sum of the first 6 terms of 2, 4, 8, ... is|126|2 (2^6 - 1)/(2 - 1) = 126."])
